The '''Confederal Aerospace Force''' or '''Confederal Air and Space Force''' ('''CASF'''; {{lang-bl|La Fuercia Aérea y Espacial}}) is the combined [[W:air force|air]], [[w:outer space|space]], and [[W:Intercontinental ballistic missile|strategic]]/tactical missile [[w:military branch|service branch]] of the [[Confederal Armed Forces]]. Additionally, it is one of the five uniformed services of the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Originally established in 1928, the Air Force incorporated the [[Confederal Aerospace Command]] on 16 May 1963, from which it explored the feasibility of low-orbit [[w:Anti-satellite weapon|anti-satellite missiles]] and other [[w:Space weapons|space weapons]] in order to achieve a comprehensive [[w:Missile defense|missile defense system]].

It is currently dedicated to missile defense, aerospace warning, air and space sovereignty, and other related protection for the Baliscan archipelago and Baliscan owned in-[[w:Orbit|orbit]] objects, such as [[w:Reconnaissance satellite|reconnaissance satellites]]. Additionally, the Confederal Air and Space Force participates in the development and upkeep of the [[SAN (satellite navigation)|SAN satellite navigation system]]. The branch also has an {{W|aerobatic}} team known as [[Azure Arrows]] and has provided air transport in UN peacekeeping missions. It is also heavily involved in international {{W|humanitarian assistance}} and evacuations, having most recently participated in the {{W|2021 Kabul airlift}}.

The 2017 [[Confederal Defense Allocation]] adopted by the [[Confederal Congress]] merged the [[Confederal Missile Defence Force]] and the Strategic Command into the fold of the Confederal Air Force, eventually transitioning into a fully combined aerial and spatial branch. The organization shares control of the [[Maravíes Aerospace Center]] with the Baliscan [[AXA|Aerospace Exploration Agency]] (AXA), which it cooperates with extensively.

Balisca has the 3rd largest land-based missile arsenal in the world. This includes 800 conventionally armed short-range [[W:Ballistic missile|ballistic missiles]], 200 to 300 conventional medium-range ballistic missiles and an unknown number of conventional intermediate-range ballistic missiles, hundreds of [[W:Hypersonic missile|hypersonic missiles]] and [[W:Hypersonic glide vehicle|glide vehicles]], as well as 200-300 ground-launched [[W:Cruise missile|cruise missiles]].

